      "id": "hackernews-2026-07-17-manufact-yc-s25-is-hiring-a-senior-infra-engineer-to-build-t",
      "title": "Manufact (YC S25) Is Hiring a Senior infra engineer to build the MCP cloud",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/manufact/jobs/Dh6PYP5-senior-infrastructure-engineer\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48947100\nPoints: 0\n# Comments: 0",
      "body": "Cloud infrastructure for MCP servers and Claude / ChatGPT apps.Senior Infrastructure Engineer$100K - $180K•0.10% - 0.70%•San Francisco, CA, US / RemoteSkillsAmazon Web Services (AWS), Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud, TypeScriptConnect directly with founders of the best YC-funded startups.Apply to role ›About the roleAbout us\nManufact is Vercel for MCP.\nWe are building the MCP cloud platform to get any product ready for Claude Connectors marketplace, ChatGPT App Store and any AI agent that supports MCP.\nManufact Cloud usage is more than doubling every month.\nWe're the team behind mcp-use SDK (next.js for MCP), the open-source framework for building MCP Apps with 10k Github stars and 8M+ downloads across python and typescript.\nUsed by 20% of US 500 like NASA, SAP, NVIDIA and more than 5,000 companies.\nWe raised $6.3M seed in 4 days before YC demo day. Our lead investor is PeakXV (best dev-tools VC out there), and we have the best angels, including the founders of Supabase.\nOur focus: capture a significant share of global AI tool calls that flow through Manufact.\nBuild the cloud platform that hosts customer MCP servers with millions of tool calls.\nSet up monitoring, observability, and dashboards across every MCP server on Manufact Cloud and the full stream of events and logs we ingest, so problems surface before users feel them.\nBuild alerting and error handling that flags threshold breaches and failures in real time.\nMake sure the platform scales as we add thousands of users and capture a growing share of global AI tool calls.\nCreate the tooling and technical blueprints that let customers deploy Manufact into their own private clouds (AWS, Azure, GCP) on their own terms.\nBuild the security boundaries that keep each customer's data private and isolated within their own environment.\nOwn where our code lives and how it ships: code hosting and the release pipeline.\nKeep the system fast and reliable as companies add more MCP servers.\nYou have built and operated cloud systems end-to-end and know them inside out.\nExperience standing up the observability stack that keeps a cloud healthy: logs, metrics, traces, dashboards, and alerting at scale.\nKubernetes or Terraform, and containerized multi-tenant systems.\nComfortable being the first person to own infrastructure at a fast-growing startup.\nBased in or willing to relocate to San Francisco.\nHands-on with observability tooling such as ClickHouse, Prometheus, OpenTelemetry, Grafana.\nExperience running a platform that others deploy onto (PaaS-flavored).\nTell us about infrastructure you've built and operated, and share URLs, writeups, or repos.\nIntro call with a founder.\nDesign exercise: architect the hosting plus observability layer for a platform like Manufact Cloud, then walk through it with the team.\nPaid trial with the team.\nAbout ManufactManufact provides open-source dev tools and infrastructure for MCP to help dev teams quickly build and deploy MCP Servers for AI agents & MCP Apps for ChatGPT and Claude.\nWe developed the mcp-use SDK, which has over 7M downloads and 10,000 GitHub stars, and is used by 20% of the US 500.\nCreate MCP servers/apps in minutes, connect your GitHub repo, and make them immediately available to AI agents and ChatGPT.Founded:2025Batch:S25Team Size:5Status:ActiveLocation:San FranciscoFounders",
