      "id": "theverge-2026-07-16-new-york-governor-says-she-8217-s-using-ai-to-analyze-8216-e",
      "title": "New York governor says she&#8217;s using AI to analyze &#8216;every single rule&#8217; in the state",
      "summary": "New York Governor Kathy Hochul might have just signed a moratorium on new AI data centers in the state, but she's not against using the technology herself. During an interview with Bloomberg's Odd Lots podcast, Hochul said that her team is using \"AI to analyze every single rule, regulation, [and] policy\" to check for outdated legislation.\nSome of the antiquated laws mentioned by Hochul in the inte",
      "body": "New York Governor Kathy Hochul might have just signed a moratorium on new AI data centers in the state, but she’s not against using the technology herself. During an interview with Bloomberg’s Odd Lots podcast, Hochul said that her team is using “AI to analyze every single rule, regulation, [and] policy” to check for outdated legislation.\nSome of the antiquated laws mentioned by Hochul in the interview include a $25 fee required to take a dog hunting, or a stipulation that pregnant people need a permit to work after midnight. Hochul added that it “probably would have taken five years at the staff level” to review all of the laws in the state, but with AI, her team “did it in a couple of months.” This will allow Hochul and state agencies “to get rid of” these outdated regulations, she said.&nbsp;\nEarlier this week, New York became the first state to put a pause on new hyperscale data centers for up to a year. In the meantime, state lawmakers plan to come up with regulations to protect residents from the rising utility costs and the threat to natural resources posed by massive data centers.\n“I want a government that’s not on your back but on your side, and using AI has been powerful to do that,” Hochul told Bloomberg. “I think every level of government should use this… I’m going to make dramatic changes using the power of AI.”",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "AI",
        "News",
        "Policy",
        "Politics"
      ],
      "author": "Emma Roth",
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-16T17:58:37.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/07/gettyimages-2283395662.jpg?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0,10.727373918039,100,78.545252163922",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theverge.com/ai-artificial-intelligence/966647/new-york-governor-kathy-hochul-ai-policies",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
    },
    {
      "id": "theverge-2026-07-16-ecovacs-8217-self-cleaning-deebot-x11-has-hit-a-new-low-pric",
      "title": "Ecovacs&#8217; self-cleaning Deebot X11 has hit a new low price",
      "summary": "Sometimes it feels like keeping your floors clean is one of those never-ending chores, which is why it's nice to have a versatile robot vacuum take it off your hands. The Ecovacs Deebot X11 robovac / mop hybrid is designed to do just that, and it's now $699 ($400 off) at Amazon and directly from Ecovacs, which is a new low price. \nThe Deebot X11 is the latest version of one of our former top picks",
      "body": "Sometimes it feels like keeping your floors clean is one of those never-ending chores, which is why it’s nice to have a versatile robot vacuum take it off your hands. The Ecovacs Deebot X11 robovac / mop hybrid is designed to do just that, and it’s now $699 ($400 off) at Amazon and directly from Ecovacs, which is a new low price.&nbsp;\nThe Deebot X11 is the latest version of one of our former top picks for the best robot vacuum / mop. While the Matic has since taken its place in our rankings, the X11 remains an excellent option, especially at nearly half the price. It combines powerful 19,500Pa suction along with a handful of features that make cleaning feel nearly effortless, including lidar and a 3D camera that help it map your home and avoid obstacles. The extending roller mop reaches farther into corners and along edges, and automatically lifts itself to help keep rugs dry. Plus, mechanical levers help the robot get over thicker rugs, raised doorways, and uneven floors more easily.\n[Product: Ecovacs Deebot X11 OmniCyclone  | https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FJRZGDNY?tag=theverge02-20, https://www.anrdoezrs.net/links/8836598/type/dlg/https://www.ecovacs.com/us/shop/deebot-robotic-vacuum-cleaner/deebot-x11-omnicyclone]\nMaintenance is minimal, too. Every time the robot returns to its dock to rinse the mop, it also quickly tops off the battery, making it less likely to pause for a long break midway through a cleaning session. The bagless dock automatically empties the dustbin, then washes the mop with hot water and dries it. It also supports Matter, so you can control the bot using your voice via any major smart home platform instead of having to get up or even reach for your phone.",
      "source": "The Verge",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [
        "Gadgets",
        "Smart Home",
        "Tech",
        "Verge Shopping"
      ],
      "author": "Sheena Vasani",
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-16T17:57:15.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/07/ecovacsomnicyclone11deebots.webp?quality=90&strip=all&crop=0,10.403009371288,100,79.193981257424",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.theverge.com/gadgets/966651/ecovacs-deebot-x11-robot-vacuum-deal-sale",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
