      "id": "bbc-2026-07-16-bellingham-slapped-argentina-substitute-after-england-exit",
      "title": "Bellingham slapped Argentina substitute after England exit",
      "summary": "Jude Bellingham sparks melee as he slaps Argentina substitute Valentin Barco on the back of the head following England's 2-1 World Cup semi-final defeat.",
      "body": "Lautaro Martinez headed the winner for Argentina in the second minute of stoppage time, ending the hopes of an England side who had taken an early second-half lead through Anthony Gordon's goal.Barco, 21, who plays for French side Strasbourg and previously had a spell at Brighton, is expected to join Chelsea.He has featured once at the tournament as a second-half substitute in a 3-1 group win against Jordan.The first half of Wednesday's match in Atlanta was feisty with 19 fouls, as American referee Ismail Elfath struggled to keep control.Bellingham, who has scored six goals in the tournament, also had a confrontation with Argentina captain Lionel Messi in the fourth minute after England midfielder Elliot Anderson had been fouled.\"We were really just discussing a foul, actually,\" Bellingham is reported to have said. after the match.\"It wasn't anything bad. I'm sure everyone will do their thing and make it a big deal, but it was nothing.\"",
      "source": "BBC",
      "category": "world",
      "tags": [],
      "author": null,
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-16T08:38:33.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://ichef.bbci.co.uk/ace/branded_sport/1200/cpsprodpb/bd04/live/6ce52a20-80e5-11f1-b976-0b9c15b0ccfc.jpg",
      "originalUrl": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/c74glwpv99yo?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
    },
