      "id": "hackernews-2026-07-15-grok-build-is-open-source",
      "title": "Grok Build is open source",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://github.com/xai-org/grok-build\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48926590\nPoints: 410\n# Comments: 432",
      "body": "Grok Build is SpaceXAI's terminal-based AI coding agent. It runs as a\nfull-screen TUI that understands your codebase, edits files, executes shell\ncommands, searches the web, and manages long-running tasks — interactively,\nheadlessly for scripting/CI, or embedded in editors via the Agent Client\nInstalling the released binary ·\nLearn more about Grok Build at x.ai/cli\nThis repository contains the Rust source for the grok CLI/TUI and its agent\nruntime. It is synced periodically from the SpaceXAI monorepo.\nPrebuilt binaries are published for macOS, Linux, and Windows:\ncurl -fsSL https://x.ai/cli/install.sh | bash   # macOS / Linux / Git Bash\nirm https://x.ai/cli/install.ps1 | iex          # Windows PowerShell\nSee the changelog for the latest fixes,\nfeatures, and improvements in each release.\nRust — the toolchain is pinned by rust-toolchain.toml;\nrustup installs it automatically on first build.\nprotoc — proto codegen resolves bin/protoc (a\ndotslash launcher) or falls back to a protoc on\nmacOS and Linux are supported build hosts; Windows builds are best-effort\nand not currently tested from this tree.\ncargo run -p xai-grok-pager-bin              # build + launch the TUI\ncargo build -p xai-grok-pager-bin --release  # release binary: target/release/xai-grok-pager\ncargo check -p xai-grok-pager-bin            # fast validation\nThe binary artifact is named xai-grok-pager; official installs ship it as\ngrok. On first launch it opens your browser to authenticate — see the\nFull online documentation is available at\nThe user guide ships with the pager crate:\n— getting started, keyboard shortcuts, slash commands, configuration, theming,\nMCP servers, skills, plugins, hooks, headless mode, sandboxing, and more.\nComposition-root package; builds the xai-grok-pager binary\nThe TUI: scrollback, prompt, modals, rendering\nAgent runtime + leader/stdio/headless entry points\nTool implementations (terminal, file edit, search, ...)\nHost filesystem, VCS, execution, checkpoints\nThe rest of the CLI crate closure (config, MCP, markdown, sandbox, ...)\nSmall shared leaf crates pulled in by the closure\nVendored upstream source (Mermaid diagram stack) — see below\nImportantThe root Cargo.toml (workspace members, dependency versions, lints,\nprofiles) is generated — treat it as read-only. Prefer editing per-crate\ncargo check -p <crate>        # always target specific crates; full-workspace builds are slow\ncargo test -p xai-grok-config # per-crate tests\ncargo clippy -p <crate>       # lint config: clippy.toml at the repo root\ncargo fmt --all               # rustfmt.toml at the repo root\nFirst-party code in this repository is licensed under the Apache License,\nVersion 2.0 — see LICENSE.\nThird-party and vendored code remains under its original licenses. See:\nTHIRD-PARTY-NOTICES — crates.io / git dependencies,\nbundled UI themes, and in-tree source ports (including openai/codex and\n— crate-local notice for the codex and opencode ports (license texts +\nthird_party/NOTICE — vendored Mermaid-stack index",
      "source": "Hacker News",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "skp1995",
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-15T20:24:58.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130314967?s=400&v=4",
