      "id": "techcrunch-2026-07-15-microsoft-patches-bug-in-video-game-age-of-empires-ii",
      "title": "Microsoft patches bug in video game Age of Empires II",
      "summary": "The vulnerability in the decades-old game could have allowed hackers to take over victims’ computers with a malicious game invite.",
      "body": "11:47 AM PDT · July 15, 2026\nOn Tuesday, Microsoft patched a historic record number of security bugs across its product lines, in large part due to the use of AI to help the company and external researchers discover bugs.\nAmong the fixed vulnerabilities was one for the remastered version of the classic 25-year-old war strategy video game Age of Empires II. The flaw allowed hackers to take over a victim’s computer by sending a custom malicious game invite, according to security researchers.\nA video posted on X shows how the flaw could be exploited by hackers.\nHere’s the Age of Empires RCE from yesterday’s Patch Tuesday: CVE-2026-50663.Join an attacker’s lobby, (auto-)accept UCG, and you get  remote code execution. pic.twitter.com/QmMkY07C8S— Rick de Jager (@rdjgr) July 15, 2026\nAccording to cybersecurity firm Rapid7, a successful attack would have allowed hackers to place malicious files on the victim’s computer, opening the door for the hacker to achieve the ability to run malicious code on the victim’s machine.\nThat means, effectively, the hacker could have taken over control of the hacked computer.\nThere is no evidence that this bug was successfully exploited in the wild by hackers. But targeting video gamers can be an effective way to install malware on a high number of victims’ computers and steal their passwords, for example.\nSubscribe for the industry’s biggest tech news",
      "source": "TechCrunch",
      "category": "tech",
      "tags": [],
      "author": "Lorenzo Franceschi-Bicchierai",
      "publishedAt": "2026-07-15T18:47:01.000Z",
      "imageUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/age-of-empires-ii-microsoft.jpg?resize=1200,675",
      "originalUrl": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/15/microsoft-patches-bug-in-video-game-age-of-empires-ii/",
      "readTimeMinutes": 1,
      "language": "en"
